  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Concrete Pumping is benefiting from robust demand in heavy commercial and infrastructure work—particularly data centers, roads, bridges, and energy projects—which more than offsets lingering softness in light commercial and residential segments. Eco-Pan waste services are adding organic growth. Recent acquisitions in Ireland and the U.K. diversify end-market exposure. While the operational momentum is strong, the stock’s elevated valuation and thin liquidity are injecting a note of caution into the narrative.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management raised its full-year outlook after another strong quarter, signaling confidence in the trajectory. The U.K. and Ireland acquisitions complement organic expansion, though integration risks remain a concern for some market participants. Execution has been steady and the demand backdrop is supportive, but analyst targets suggest the share price may have run ahead of fundamentals, tempering enthusiasm despite the solid operational delivery.",
